 "notes": "Combined 95% C.L. upper limit on the photon-paraphoton mixing angle chi ('our experiment' curve, Fig. 4), recovered from the vector paths of the ROOT-generated limit.eps in the arXiv e-print. Axis calibration cross-checked: extracted worst spike at m=1.396 eV (paper quotes chi_worst=8.01e-5 at 1.39 eV; that quoted point is included explicitly since the narrow plotted spike undershoots slightly at pixel resolution). Plateau chi=3.86e-5 above ~0.1 eV; extended flat to 26 keV following the dashed continuation line in Fig. 4 and the paper's stated validity range (0.04 eV < m < 26 keV; below 0.04 eV the plotted curve rises as m^-2 up to chi~1 at m~3.5e-4 eV and is included as drawn). LSW laboratory experiment: no dark-matter density assumption, no rescaling applied. The paper's conservative single-number headline is chi < 8.06e-5 (95% C.L.) over the full range; the reported curve is the actual mass-dependent combined limit as plotted.",
